A||||6||Drapes85Fiero||Headlight prob not the motor||||4||
Z||000000||Drapes85Fiero||05-20-2000||11:52 AM||||  Ok I have a slight problem.  When I hit the headlight switch the lights come up but they don't come on.  The parking lights come on, and I have checked the fuse for the the lights and they look good.  I took the switch out and looked at it and pluged it back in but it still won't work.  The lights are pretty new about 2 years old so I'm pretty sure that thier not bad.  any suggestions would be nice<BR>  Drapes||||reg||4
Z||000001||V8Fiero||05-20-2000||12:00 PM||||I had a headlight that wouldnt come up till I just started to turn the knob on top, then it would come up by itself. What I did was take the headlight motor out, took off the side panel ( the one with the 3 screws ) this gives you access to the brushes. I then cleaned the brushes off. It worked like a charm. You might want to give this a try. <P>Hope it helps.<BR>||||reg||6
Z||000002||V8Fiero||05-20-2000||12:07 PM||||OOOpps. I suppose it would help if I read the problem a little better. hehe <P><BR>Did you try looking at the 3 prong plug on the back of the light? Sometimes those get corroded. If that doesnt work what I would suggest is to take a test light to see if you are getting power to the plug. If not you've either got a fuse blown or a bad wire somewhere.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Drapes85Fiero||05-20-2000||12:28 PM||||  Ok I did some more troubleshooting its seems that the Hi beams work so now I'm more lost than before. I messed with the dimmer switch and still no lights ||||reg||4
Z||000004||theogre||05-20-2000||05:07 PM||||disconnect the dimmer switch.<P>turn on the lights.<P>put a test light or volt meter with one lead gounded in each of the dimmer connector holes. One of them should light the tester or show voltage on the meter. If the tester doesn't light is the main switch of something connected to it.<P>Now jumper that "hot" terminal to one of the other 2. The headlights should come on. if the do move the jumper between the hot lead and  the last terminal. do they light now?<P>if you got one beam with the jumper but not the other then it's a wire problem.<P>if the both beams work with the jumper the dimmer switch is bad.<P>if the test light worked, but neither beam worked with the jumper then the lights have moselikely lost their ground.<p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 05-20-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||Drapes85Fiero||05-20-2000||11:57 PM||||Ok I used my factory manual and found that the Light green wire is shorted to ground I used my multimeter and verified.  Ok now I have another prob do I have to change out the entire harness or is there another way?||||reg||1
Z||000006||Monkeyman||05-21-2000||12:56 PM||||I have no idea if you have to change the entire harness (seems unlikely to me), but if you do, spend the extra money and upgrade to the later style headlight motors.  Better, quieter motors and a heck of a lot cheaper to rebuild.||||reg||1
